# Python
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/
*.egg

# OpenAstro runtime
*.db-journal
*.svg
!icons/**/*.svg
tmp/

# Chart exports (PNG, JPG, PDF) contain birth data
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.pdf

# SQLite databases. The two OpenAstro atlases are kept in the repo:
#   famous.sql    (~364 KB, famous-people database)
#   geonames.sql  (~31 MB, offline city atlas)
# Runtime and exported databases (astrodb.sql, peopledb.sql, chart exports,
# journals) stay out.
*.sql
*.db
!famous.sql
!geonames.sql

# OS
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Backup files and Dropbox conflict copies (English and Spanish names)
*~
old/
*.bak
*conflicted copy*
*Copia en conflicto*

# Local working files, deliberately out of the repo:
#   AGENTS.md  agent coordination notes — contains absolute local paths
#   TODO.md    pending-features roadmap. Kept out because it quotes the
#              reverse-engineering sources, including sample records from
#              third-party files. The sample was anonymised on 2026-09-21,
#              but check before ever moving this into the repo rather than
#              trusting this line.
#   README     leftover from upstream; the real one is README.md
AGENTS.md
TODO.md
/README
# Everything under .claude except the agent definitions and the hook wiring,
# which are project documentation with nothing personal in them. Losing those
# with a wiped .claude would mean rebuilding the setup from memory. Note the
# pattern excludes the *contents*, not the directory: git does not descend
# into an excluded directory, so `.claude/` plus a negation would not work.
.claude/*
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/settings.json
.claude/worktrees/
